[h1]D'thorga Farming[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.8.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published yet - draft held for the owner's review

[h2]Read this first (gotchas)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Not yet tested in game.[/b] Everything here is built and checked offline, and read from the game's and the mods' code.
[*][b]Needs Vehicle Framework and D'thorga Framework[/b] (0.202.0 or later), on [b]RimWorld 1.7 only[/b]. Load it after both. The mod asks for that order itself, so RimSort sorts it for you.
[*][b]A combine has no front until you fit one.[/b] Research mechanised harvesting, build the Reaper combine harvester (Architect > D'thorga > Farming), then fit the standard grain front from its upgrades. Without a front it refuses to harvest and says why.
[*][b]Mark the field first.[/b] Select a growing zone and press Machine-worked. Colonists then keep off it, unless Hands may help is on.
[*][b]Tractors do nothing alone.[/b] They carry or pull an implement, and an implement or a cart moves only on a hitch. Research tillage and sowing (and articulated tractors for the T400), build a Thane tractor and an implement, and hitch it. Then the Plough, Cultivate or Sow a paddock order appears.
[*][b]The Thane T400 is built in two halves.[/b] Its blueprint is the front half: leave room behind it, where the rear half is set down when it is finished.
[*][b]A seed drill needs seed in its hopper:[/b] the crop's own grain kept back from a harvest, or seed grain bought from bulk goods traders.
[*][b]Each front cuts only the crops it really could.[/b] The grain fronts take cereals, pulses and oilseeds; the corn header takes corn and sunflowers. Potatoes, hay and cotton need harvesters that come later, and stay for hands. With Vanilla Cooking Expanded, wheat, barley, oats, rye and sorghum stay for hands too, as they give flour straight from the plant.
[*][b]A combine's tank holds one kind of grain at a time.[/b] With another crop's grain still in it, it refuses the paddock and says so: pour it out first.
[*][b]A full combine needs somewhere to empty:[/b] a Garner chaser bin parked near the paddock, a field bin, or a grain silo. The silo keeps grain four times as long, [b]but only while its fan has power[/b]. [b]Empty a bin or silo before taking it down.[/b]
[*][b]Settings to decide before you start[/b] (Options > Mod settings > D'thorga Farming): Hands may help on new paddocks (off), A machine's driver can fail a harvest, as by hand (on), and Hands use seed too (off). With The Dead Man's Switch - Legion, also Agricultural Frame: hay only from straw crops (on).
[*][b]Safe to add to a running colony.[/b]
[*][b]Removing it:[/b] paddocks become plain growing zones, and every combine, tractor, implement, chaser bin, field bin and silo vanishes with the mod, with the grain and seed in them. Empty them first.
[/list]

[h2]What it does[/h2]
Machines that work your fields. Mark a growing zone as a paddock, and tractors plough, cultivate and sow it, and a combine harvester cuts it, row by row, by themselves.

[list]
[*][b]Tractors[/b] in three sizes, from 60 to 400 kW (the largest bends in the middle), carry a turnover plough or a cultivator on a three-point linkage and pull a seed drill. Ploughing clears weeds and wild plants, never a sown crop.
[*][b]The Reaper combine harvester[/b] lays the paddock out in rows and cuts every ripe plant its front covers. Unripe plants are left standing. The driver's harvesting skill sets the yield, as it does by hand. With nobody aboard, it calls a colonist with Drive work.
[*][b]When its tank is full[/b] it drives to the nearest chaser bin, field bin or silo with room, empties it through its auger, and goes back to the rows.
[*][b]Grain is held by weight[/b], not in stacks, and it weighs on the engine that carries it. Pour it onto the ground, where colonists haul it as usual, or into another bin.
[*][b]How much each holds:[/b] combine 9 tonnes of one crop (12 with the tank extension), chaser bin 12 tonnes, field bin 25 tonnes, silo 60 tonnes.
[*][b]Upgrades:[/b] tyre ballast, front weights, dual wheels and a saddle tank on the tractors; wing extensions on every implement and a bigger hopper on the drill; a tank extension and a straw chopper on the combine, and a fast auger on the chaser bin.
[/list]

Every figure is authored, to tune in play. Other mods' crops are taken once they are placed in a crop class, with one short patch each; [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-rimworld/blob/main/docs/modding/farming.md]the page for modders[/url] shows how.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.7
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3014915404]Vehicle Framework[/url]
[*]D'thorga Framework, 0.202.0 or later
[/list]
Optional: Vanilla Cooking Expanded and Vanilla Plants Expanded, whose crops are sorted for the fronts.

[h2]Credits[/h2]
The machines' pictures are AI-generated and picked by hand. The tractors' engine sounds are real recordings, cut and levelled: a Valmet tractor working a harrow (1985) by Yle, the Finnish Broadcasting Company's archive (YleArkisto on Freesound, CC BY 4.0), and a Case IH CX90's engine stopping by Soundholder on Freesound (CC BY 3.0), with thanks to mickyman5000, kyles and bruno.auzet on Freesound, whose recordings are CC0.

